# DataTables Actions Pattern

## Standard Action Column Template

This template provides a consistent pattern for action buttons in DataTables across the application.

### Key Features:
- **Centered alignment**: Uses flexbox for perfect center alignment
- **Permission-based**: Each action respects Laravel's Gate permissions
- **Consistent styling**: Uses standard Bootstrap and Tabler icons
- **Responsive spacing**: Proper margins and padding for mobile/desktop

```blade
{{-- Action column template for DataTables --}}
<div class="d-flex justify-content-center align-items-center">
    {{-- Custom action example: Edit sentiment with JavaScript handler --}}
    <a href="javascript:;" class="text-body edit-sentiment" data-id="{{ $contact->id }}">
        <i class="ti ti-mood-happy ti-sm me-2"></i>
    </a>
    
    {{-- Commented out actions can be enabled as needed --}}
    {{-- <a href="#" class="text-body"><i class="ti ti-message-chatbot ti-sm me-2"></i></a> --}}
    
    {{-- Conditional action: Only show if user has edit permission --}}
    @if (auth()->user()->can('contact.edit'))
        {{-- State-dependent action: Different display based on model state --}}
        @if ($contact->isInList60())
            {{-- Read-only state: Shows success icon without action --}}
            <a class="text-success"><i class="ti ti-list-check ti-sm me-2"></i></a>
        @else
            {{-- Interactive state: Clickable action with JavaScript handler --}}
            <a href="#" class="text-body" onclick="addToList({{ $contact->id }}, this)">
                <i class="ti ti-list-check ti-sm me-2"></i>
            </a>
        @endif
    @endif
    
    {{-- Standard view/edit action: Links to resource show page --}}
    @if (auth()->user()->can('contact.show'))
        <a href="{{ route('contact.show', $contact->id) }}" class="text-body">
            <i class="ti ti-edit ti-sm me-2"></i>
        </a>
    @endif
    
    {{-- Destructive action: Delete with confirmation and danger styling --}}
    @if (auth()->user()->can('contact.destroy'))
        <a href="#" class="text-danger" onclick="deleteRecord({{ $contact->id }}, this)">
            <i class="ti ti-trash ti-sm"></i>
        </a>
    @endif
</div>
```

### Design Guidelines:

#### **Icon Standards:**
- Use **ti-sm** size for action icons (consistent across all tables)
- Apply **me-2** margin for proper spacing between icons
- Use semantic colors: `text-body` (default), `text-success`, `text-danger`

#### **Permission Pattern:**
- Always wrap actions in permission checks: `@if (auth()->user()->can('model.action'))`
- Use descriptive permission names: `model.show`, `model.edit`, `model.destroy`

#### **JavaScript Integration:**
- Use `href="javascript:;"` for JavaScript-only actions
- Pass model ID as data attribute or function parameter
- Include confirmation dialogs for destructive actions

#### **State Management:**
- Show different icons/colors based on model state
- Disable actions when not applicable (read-only states)
- Provide visual feedback for current states

