## Disable Row Selection in DataTables

To prevent table rows from being selectable by users, use one of these methods:

### Method 1: DataTables Parameters (Recommended)

This approach disables selection at the DataTables level and applies CSS to prevent text selection:

```php
->parameters([
    'select' => false, // Disable DataTables row selection feature
    'autoWidth' => false,
    'drawCallback' => 'function() {
        // Apply CSS to prevent text selection on table rows
        $("#TABLE_ID tbody tr").css({
            "user-select": "none",           // Standard CSS property
            "-webkit-user-select": "none",   // WebKit browsers (Chrome, Safari)
            "-moz-user-select": "none",      // Firefox
            "-ms-user-select": "none"        // Internet Explorer/Edge
        });
    }',
])
```

### Method 2: Global CSS (Alternative)

Apply styles globally to all DataTables:

```css
.dataTable tbody tr {
    user-select: none;
    -webkit-user-select: none;
    -moz-user-select: none;
    -ms-user-select: none;
}
```

### When to Use:
- **Action-only tables**: When rows should not be selectable for bulk operations
- **Read-only displays**: When selection would confuse the user experience
- **Mobile optimization**: To prevent accidental text selection on touch devices
